// The NetClient domain of the client binding: a message in flight, as the NetClient seams read it.
//
// Row shapes: see binding.def, which documents them. A `message` is the CDataStore the client
// passes to NetClient::ProcessMessage or NetClient::Send, positioned at its opcode: the bytes
// from m_read to m_size are the message, and m_data is the buffer they live in. Nothing here
// writes: a mod that wants the message not to happen suppresses it at the seam.
